            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Domestic Policy and the \"Jamahiriya\" System</strong><br>\nGaddafi introduced the \"Jamahiriya,\" or \"state of the masses,\" in Libya, which he claimed was a form of direct democracy, though in practice it was considered authoritarian, with power concentrated in his hands.</p>\n\n<p><strong>c1</strong><br>\nEarly Life and Education</p>\n\n<p><strong>Pol Pot, born Saloth Sar on May 19, 1925, in Kampong Thum Province, Cambodia, studied radio electronics in Paris. During his time in France, he became involved in the communist movement and joined the French Communist Party.</strong><br>\nReturn to Cambodia and Rise in the Party</p>\n"
              },
